  "description": "Westlake features a Solum Series hybrid frame that features Rider Optimized Geometry specifically designed to assure a proper and comfortable fit. The word Solum refers to the upper layer of a soil profile, which means that in addition to its on asphalt commuting skills it can also venture out onto that upper layer of soil that presents itself as unpaved lake and fire roads. Westlake is versatile and features a Suntour NEX HLO suspension fork with just the right amount of travel for dual sport riding. The suspension fork absorbs small bumps off road, and has a hydraulic lockout that allows you to make the fork rigid minimizing bounce and maximizing the energy from your pedaling efforts. Westlake comes complete with a Shimano 24 speed drive train that includes EZ Fire shifters. Its wheelset is made from Pivit alloy 28h disc hubs laced to DC-26 700c alloy double wall rims and reliable all weather stopping is made possible courtesy of a pair of Shimano M315 hydraulic disc brakes.\nHaro Solum Dual Sport frame, Rider Optimized Geometry, hydroformed alloy tubing, chainstay disc brake mount\nSuntour NEX HLO suspension fork, 63mm travel, hydraulic lockout\nShimano TY-501 48/38/28t crankset, sealed cartridge BB\nNew Shimano ST-EF510 3x8-spd shifters w/ hydraulic levers set\nShimano M315 hydraulic disc brakeset\nTourney TY-710 front derailleur\nShimano Altus M310 rear derailleur\nPivit disc brake hubs w/ Alex DC-26 700c DW rims\nPivit alloy 25mm riser bar and forged stem\nKenda Bitumen 700 x 38c tires",
